Keep the QSV scaler width even: vpp_qsv rejects w=-2, so w=-1 could round to
an odd width (1280x720 to h=384 gives 683) while the encoder uses the profile's
even 682.  An odd width has no 4:2:0 chroma plane and hung the Apollolake media
engine (i915 "Hang on vcs0" in tvh:sharer, hevc_qsv), wedging tvheadend.

Proposed on top of patch 100 (tvheadend#2117); not in uknunknown's branch yet.

--- src/transcoding/transcode/hwaccels/qsv.c.orig
+++ src/transcoding/transcode/hwaccels/qsv.c
@@ -131,8 +131,20 @@ static int set_hwframe_ctx(AVCodecContext *ctx, AVBufferRef *hw_device_ctx)
 
 static int qsv_get_scale_filter(AVCodecContext *iavctx, int height, char *filter, size_t filter_len)
 {
-    // NOTE: vpp_qsv does not accept -2 (but -1 does the same thing)
-    if (str_snprintf(filter, filter_len, "w=-1:h=%d:scale_mode=2", height)){
+    const TVHContext *ctx = iavctx->opaque;
+    const int width = ((TVHVideoCodecProfile *)ctx->profile)->size.num;
+
+    // NOTE: vpp_qsv does not accept -2, and -1 rounds to the nearest width,
+    // which can be odd: 1280x720 scaled to h=384 gives 683.  An odd width
+    // has no 4:2:0 chroma plane and has been seen to hang the media engine
+    // (i915 "Hang on vcs0" while encoding hevc_qsv).  The profile already
+    // holds the even width the encoder is configured with, so ask vpp_qsv
+    // for exactly that; -1 stays the fallback when it is unknown.
+    if (width > 0) {
+        if (str_snprintf(filter, filter_len, "w=%d:h=%d:scale_mode=2", width, height)) {
+            return -1;
+        }
+    } else if (str_snprintf(filter, filter_len, "w=-1:h=%d:scale_mode=2", height)) {
         return -1;
     }
     return 0;
